    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><em>You are where several futures agree to meet.</em></p><p>Once per <strong>a Soma Break</strong>, as an <strong>action</strong>, you can unfold a Convergence Horizon for <strong>1 minute</strong>.</p><ul><li>Whenever a creature within <strong>6 squares</strong> of you makes an attack roll, attribute check, or defense check, you may use your reaction to let them <strong>roll an additional 2d10x10</strong> and choose which result to use.</li><li>You can do this a number of times equal to your <strong>tier</strong> during the duration.</li><li>In addition, enemies within 6 squares that <strong>critically succeed</strong> on an attack or check against your party must reroll the 2d10x10 and take the second result instead, as their best-case outcomes slide away from them.</li></ul><p><strong>OP / Campaign Echo.</strong> If a major battle, Spark operation, or faction crisis resolved under the Convergence Horizon ends with a <strong>Justice/Reformation</strong> or <strong>Liberation</strong> style outcome instead of Subjugation or Ruin, your faction may gain <strong>+1 Unity OP</strong>, <strong>+1 Intrigue OP</strong>, and reduce <strong>Darkness</strong> by 1 as word spreads of “the day everything could have gone wrong and didn’t.”</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
